\subsection{The three laws of Silent Discordance}

Based on the complete cross-graph, cross-rule experimental data, the emergence of Silent Discordance is governed by the following three laws:

% --- 修改处：第一、第三定律措辞按最新证据强度调整 ---
\textbf{First law: law of cycle enhancement.} Silent Discordance is present in both cyclic and acyclic structures, but its stability, depth, and robustness against scan resolution are enhanced by the presence of cycles. In acyclic structures (tree graphs), the valley exists but requires higher scan resolution to be resolved, and its position is determined by the geometric properties of the tree (branching number, radius). Cycles are not strictly necessary, but they enhance the phenomenon.

\textbf{Second law: law of fully symmetric interaction necessity.} Silent Discordance requires that the interaction must contain both $XX+YY$ (flip terms) and $ZZ$ (diagonal term). Under the Ising rule (chain: all-zero; random: oscillatory) and the XY rule (chain: all-zero; random: near-zero oscillatory), Silent Discordance completely disappears on all graph topologies. Under the XXZ rule, Silent Discordance persists, with the valley depth varying with the anisotropy.

\textbf{Third law: law of morphology-structure correspondence (evidence-bounded version).} The concrete morphology of Silent Discordance is jointly determined by the topology of the relation graph and the injection point of the driving force. \textbf{The only topology that currently provides strong evidence is the fractal graph, whose LDS Valley has a depth of $0.125$ ($60\%$ of curve amplitude) and has been independently replicated.} The chain graph, ring, small-world, random, and tree graphs all show a weak valley whose depth is typically $\lesssim 1.5\%$ of curve amplitude; these are reported as weak evidence pending further high-resolution studies. The star graph has been \emph{removed} from the evidence base entirely: its apparent valley at $s=1.0$ is a trivial zero arising from edge-transitive symmetry, confirmed to machine precision ($8.6\times10^{-17}$ across five Lanczos seeds), and is not Silent Discordance.

