\subsection{Relation to known physics}

The laws of Silent Discordance have no systematic counterpart in known physics. It is not a quantum phase transition, not an abrupt change of entanglement entropy, and not a simple analogue of the Edwards--Anderson spin-glass order parameter. Silent Discordance diagnoses the non-monotonic reorganization process of the relational field.

The relationship between Silent Discordance and known physics can be examined from two methodological perspectives. From an entity-first viewpoint, it may appear as a modest numerical observation in small lattice models. From a relation-first viewpoint, it is a universal dynamical signature of relational-field reorganization driven by contradiction. The present study adopts the latter, because it has successfully predicted the absence of triadic resonance on odd-numbered chains, the critical effect of contradiction-edge position, and the exact invariance under Rashba SOC.

\subsection{Symmetry-breaking-driven relational reorganization}

A unifying theme emerges: \textbf{Silent Discordance is triggered by asymmetric contradiction injection.} Symmetric driving leads to smooth adaptation. Asymmetric driving forces abrupt reorganization.

